 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? There are a few common ways. Some couples split everything fifty- fifty, no arguments. Others let the groom's family pay the entire wedding, groom's parents cover the wedding. That's a nice offer. It could be your parents' turn, or you could split it with his family. How would that feel? Not rude, but some families get touched. Would you rather talk to his parents about it, or just go with your parents' offer? Then maybe split it fifty- fifty with his family, or ask your parents not to cover anything. Weddings are your day, after all. Good idea. He' appreciate having a say.",
